8:["$","p","4",{"data-count":"","children":["On the Northeast Plain, 40.3 per cent of farmers surveyed were over 54 and only 10.6 per cent were under 35 ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","huo",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#huo","children":"Huo et al. 2022"}]]}]],")"]}],". In Lishu County in neighbouring Jilin, the average farmer surveyed was 58 ",["$","span","3",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","yu",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#yu","children":"Yu et al. 2025"}]]}]],")"]}],"."]}]
9:["$","h2","5",{"data-count":"","children":"Do machines replace people?"}]
a:["$","p","6",{"data-count":"","children":["My progress report suggested that people leave first and machines follow. This is only half right. The large, gently sloping farms suit machines, but Northeast Plain farmers ranked a lack of machinery training as their biggest barrier, and a machine costs US$1,500 to US$15,000 when cereal farmers earned under US$181.49 per hectare ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","huo",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#huo","children":"Huo et al. 2022"}]]}]],")"]}],". Many hire machine services from cooperatives instead."]}]
b:["$","p","7",{"data-count":"","children":["Only 54 per cent of the Lishu farmers had adopted conservation tillage, and some of the others were ‘informed non-adopters’ who understood it but were not convinced ",["$","span","1",{"className":"cite","children":["(",[["$","span","yu",{"children":["",["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/references/#yu","children":"Yu et al. 2025"}]]}]],")"]}],". I think this ageing, hesitant workforce is the pressure being handled least well."]}]
